WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.226
Teacher midterm practice for C plus plus, question 2.

2
00:00:04.846 --> 00:00:08.768
In the same program, what are i and sum at the moment the loop breaks?

3
00:00:10.468 --> 00:00:14.976
Fast forward to the end of pass three: i is three, and sum is twenty four.

4
00:00:15.596 --> 00:00:19.741
Pass four. Line four runs first: sum plus equals B of three,

5
00:00:19.741 --> 00:00:22.670
which is five, so sum becomes twenty nine.

6
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:27.879
Now the test: i is three, and three is greater than two, so break.

7
00:00:27.879 --> 00:00:31.659
The i plus plus on line seven never runs, so i stays three.

8
00:00:33.259 --> 00:00:36.882
The rule: inside a loop body, statements above a break run

9
00:00:36.882 --> 00:00:40.230
on the final pass, and statements below it do not.

10
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.865
That is why sum moved, but i did not.

11
00:00:44.465 --> 00:00:47.280
So at the break, i is three and sum is twenty nine.

12
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:52.061
Do not assume the loop counter is one past the last index used.

13
00:00:52.061 --> 00:00:54.721
Here the break comes before i plus plus.

14
00:00:55.441 --> 00:00:58.028
Exam tip: when a break sits in the middle of a

15
00:00:58.028 --> 00:01:01.029
loop, draw a line across the code at the break.

16
00:01:01.029 --> 00:01:04.703
On the last pass, only update the variables above that line.
